  "motif": "leaf-moon",
  "intro": "<p>Fewer names mean 'night' than you might expect, so this list also takes in names meaning evening and darkness. The best known is Layla, Arabic for night, and its many spellings: Leila, Laila and Leyla. Alongside them are Nyx and Nox, the Greek and Latin goddesses of night, Sanskrit Nisha and Yamini, and Irish names from <em>ciar</em>, 'black, dark', such as Kieran and Ciara. Every meaning is checked against a cited source, mostly Behind the Name and Wiktionary, and England and Wales ranks come from the ONS.</p><p>Night has its share of myths. Lyla, Lilah and Lila are sometimes forms of Leila and sometimes not, Lilith's link to night is an old folk etymology, and Delilah has nothing to do with it. We've marked these uncertain.</p>",
